      options: [{ key: "a", text: "The thyroid gland and laryngeal cartilage are identical" }, { key: "b", text: "Laryngeal cartilage differs from the thyroid gland" }, { key: "c", text: "The thyroid gland is an ossicle of the middle ear" }, { key: "d", text: "The thyroid cartilage alone produces thyroxine" }],
      answer: "b", explanation: "Thyroid cartilage is a laryngeal skeletal structure, whereas the thyroid gland is an endocrine organ. A frog can lack the mammalian cartilage while possessing a thyroid gland and thyroid-hormone functions.", sectionId: "frog-qualified-absences", source: { document: "biology", page: 19 }, cognitive: "understanding"
